Sweep the whole file (and any test that pins "answer key") — the term
must not survive anywhere.

## B. Figure 3 caption (fig:direct-base) — define the coverage bar, shorten

Current tail (`:512–516`):

> … marks Wikipedia's light-reviewed coverage of all \NumRefPlants{}
> reference plants (\WikiReviewedPct\%, \WikiReviewed/\NumRefPlants) — the
> answer key every model should recover, since that content sat in the
> training corpus. Models grouped on the vertical axis.

Replace from "Wikipedia's …" to the end with (author's words,
macro-sourced):

> … marks Wikipedia's coverage of \WikiReviewed{} assets
> (\WikiReviewedPct\% of our reference list) — the coverage bar that
> models could be expected to pass.

Then **END the caption** there. This drops the "answer key every model
should recover …" clause AND "Models grouped on the vertical axis."
Notes:
- Use macros `\WikiReviewed` (=130) and `\WikiReviewedPct` (=73); do not
  type the numbers.
- Em dash is the literal Unicode "—" (U+2014), never "--" (house rule).

